WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.625
Reporting is where many agencies stopped,

2
00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:06.450
so it's worth being precise about
what CISA actually receives.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.688
CISA's guidance describes
four reporting routes,

4
00:00:09.688 --> 00:00:15.163
from a CISA-hosted service that feeds the
CDM dashboard to quarterly manual uploads.

5
00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:19.489
Whatever the route, the reported
artifact is the tool's own results file,

6
00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:21.762
and agencies are told not to rename it.

7
00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:26.820
A deviation that's operationally required
shows up as Omitted, with its rationale,

8
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.762
and must be approved through the
agency's security risk process.

9
00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:35.071
CISA also supplies a template for
tracking non-compliant policies,

10
00:00:35.071 --> 00:00:37.037
planned fixes and target dates.

11
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.301
In effect, it's a plan of
action and milestones.

12
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:43.588
The directive puts the risk
decision in the right place.

13
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:48.856
Authorizing officials may accept risk for
deviations from the mandatory policies

14
00:00:48.856 --> 00:00:53.974
to meet operational needs, under agency
policy, and CISA reviews what they submit.

15
00:00:53.974 --> 00:00:55.425
Two decisions follow.

16
00:00:55.425 --> 00:00:59.613
The CISO picks the reporting route,
and the assessment operators run it.

17
00:00:59.613 --> 00:01:03.349
Operators never edit results,
and never decide omissions.

18
00:01:03.349 --> 00:01:07.849
And every deviation without an end
date goes to the authorizing official,

19
00:01:07.849 --> 00:01:11.463
because a standing omission is
a standing risk acceptance.

20
00:01:11.463 --> 00:01:13.998
The reporting floor is at least quarterly,

21
00:01:13.998 --> 00:01:17.113
so both are needed before
the next quarterly report.

22
00:01:17.113 --> 00:01:19.390
Next, the two assessment tools.
